  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Ottoman-Turkish classical art music of Istanbul court and konak salons, systematized in the makam and usul theory of Dimitrie Cantemir and Hamparsum Limonciyan and carried into republican radio practice by Münir Nurettin Selçuk and the TRT koro — heterophonic ensembles of kanun, ney, ud, kemençe and tanbur realize a single ornamented melodic line over long usul cycles from the 8-beat düyek to the 88-beat zencir, alternating composed peşrev and şarkı with improvised taksim and gazel.",
